 "reading": "Under the 24k tokenizer the full grid (7 widths, 33 runs) and the region-confined grid (3 widths, 13 runs) lead to the same adopted width: the only reliable gain lies between d = 224 and 256, inside the region, and the step to 512 was not adopted under the prospective rule. Under the 4k tokenizer the selected d = 384 is the argmax of both the full grid (4 widths, 20 runs) and the confined grid (3 widths, 15 runs). In both series the enumeration-informed region contained the width that was eventually chosen, and confining the search to it would have cost 20 fewer runs in one series and 5 in the other. This is a reading of a grid whose outcome was already known: it shows the region was not misleading, not that a practitioner could have known in advance to trust it, and the wider sweep is what established that the region was right under one tokenizer and too low under the other."
